  <div class="hw-step__body">
    <h2>Turning movies into vectors</h2>
    <p>Each movie gets a text template built from those 12 fields. Title and genres up top, plot and keywords in the middle, production details at the bottom. That template goes through <strong>Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B</strong> and comes out as 1024 numbers. A vector. Movies with similar plots and genres end up pointing in nearby directions in this high-dimensional space.</p>
    <p>The embedding run happens once on <strong>Kaggle's free dual T4 GPUs</strong>. Takes about three hours with two Qwen3 instances running side by side, one per GPU. After that the vectors are frozen. For text queries at runtime, Ollama embeds on the fly using the same model.</p>
